From 04f271fdac3425f8b68ec0cf13c7f4fa225c694f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nelson <nelson@errorware.net>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 18:03:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(providers): provider-core contract, Linode and UpCloud
 providers (ERR-42, ERR-43, ERR-44)

- crates/crow-provider-core: the provider.hosts contract (ListInstances,
  PowerControl, Snapshots) behind a Provider trait with capability
  accessors; check_declarations keeps manifests and code in agreement.
  Sync and data-shaped. HTTP is injected: CurlHttp sends the whole request,
  credentials included, on curl's stdin; tests use recorded responses.
- crates/crow-provider-linode: instances across pages, power, backup
  snapshots with an actionable message when Backups are off.
- crates/crow-provider-upcloud: servers plus addresses in two calls, soft
  power actions, token or sub-account login, no snapshots declared.
- Crow is now a workspace; providers are compiled in behind
  provider-linode / provider-upcloud features (src/providers.rs).
- Region tables learn UpCloud zones; Crow's settings manifest declares
  config.format.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
